  [PASS] F1  position-space Yukawa transmission T(r)=(1+mr)e^{-mr} is STRICTLY DECREASING: dT/dr = -m^2 r e^{-mr} < 0 for all m,r>0 -- long range is suppressed (high-pass)   (dT/dr = -m**2*r*exp(-m*r) < 0 (long-range OFF))
  [PASS] F2  Fourier transmission eta(k)=k^2/(k^2+m^2) is STRICTLY INCREASING in k: d eta/dk = 2 k m^2/(k^2+m^2)^2 > 0 -- short range (high k) passes, long range (low k) suppressed (high-pass)   (d eta/dk = 2*k*m**2/(k**4 + 2*k**2*m**2 + m**4) > 0 (short-range ON))

